# Testing

## Context

Existing tests are colocated `*.test.ts` files next to the code they cover
and run with vitest (`cd app && npm test` is green). Any new behavior (a new
reducer case, action creator, or selector) needs a colocated test written the
same way.

## Rule

- Put new tests in a `*.test.ts` file next to the module under test (e.g. a
  new reducer case gets a test in `app/src/reducer.test.ts`), not in a
  separate `__tests__/` tree.
- Structure each test in Arrange-Act-Assert order: build input state/action,
  call the function under test, assert on the result.
- Test the reducer/selectors as pure functions — do not spin up a real
  `store` just to test a reducer case.
- Every new `Action` variant or action creator needs at least one new test.

## How to verify

1. `cd app && npm test` passes with no failing or skipped tests.
2. Every new/changed `.ts` file under `app/src` has a matching `.test.ts`
   sibling covering the new behavior.
3. New tests read as Arrange/Act/Assert (setup, single call, assertion), not
   multiple unrelated actions crammed into one test.
